04:29:01.008 --> 04:29:03.544
IT ALSO APPROPRIATELY MAINTAINS

04:29:03.544 --> 04:29:04.511
FEDERAL RESPONSIBILITIES FOR

04:29:04.511 --> 04:29:06.313
HAZARDOUS SUBSTANCE CLEANUP AND

04:29:06.313 --> 04:29:08.582
OTHER OBLIGATIONS. THIS BILL

04:29:08.582 --> 04:29:09.683
REFLECTS A PRINCIPLE THAT

04:29:09.683 --> 04:29:11.385
SHOULD GUIDE FEDERAL LAND

04:29:11.385 --> 04:29:13.287
POLICY. MANAGEMENT DECISIONS

04:29:13.287 --> 04:29:14.555
SHOULD BE BASED ON THE

04:29:14.555 --> 04:29:16.056
REALITIES OF THE LANDSCAPE AND

04:29:16.056 --> 04:29:17.391
NOT SIMPLY THE BOUNDARIES DRAWN

04:29:17.391 --> 04:29:20.460
ON A MAP. DECADES AGO. OUR

04:29:20.460 --> 04:29:21.328
NATIONAL FORESTS AND PARKS

04:29:21.328 --> 04:29:22.996
SERVE MANY PURPOSES. THEY

04:29:22.996 --> 04:29:24.665
PRESERVE WILDLIFE HABITAT,

04:29:24.665 --> 04:29:26.934
PROTECT WATERSHEDS, PROVIDE

04:29:26.934 --> 04:29:29.002
RECREATION, AND SUPPORT RURAL

04:29:29.002 --> 04:29:31.138
ECONOMIES. A BALANCED APPROACH

04:29:31.138 --> 04:29:32.706
RECOGNIZES ALL OF THESE VALUES.

